# Entity CRUD — default endpoints

Every **persisted entity** (existing or new) must expose exactly these three REST operations unless explicitly exempt (see **Exemptions**). Path prefix is **`/api/v1/`** (not `/v1/api/`). Resource segment is **kebab-case plural** (`medical-departments`, `notification-rules`).

Wire JSON: PascalCase envelope and DTO keys (`api-json-pascal-case.mdc`). User-facing `Message`/`Title`: server-localized (`server-message-i18n.mdc`).

## 1. List — `GET /api/v1/{entityName}`

Paginated list of entity rows.

| Query param | Default | Notes |
|-------------|---------|-------|
| `page` | `0` | Zero-based page index |
| `size` | `20` | Cap at 100 in service layer |
| `sort` | entity-specific | Optional; e.g. `createdAt,desc` |
| `Query` | — | Optional JSON object (URL-encoded) whose keys match filterable entity attributes |

**Query object:** Accept a structured filter DTO (`{Entity}QueryDto`) bound from request params. Every optional field maps to an entity attribute (exact or case-insensitive match per field). Also support a URL-encoded JSON `Query` param for clients that send a single object, e.g. `?page=0&size=20&Query=%7B%22Code%22%3A%22CARD%22%7D`. Reject unknown or non-filterable keys with `400` + stable `ErrorCode`.

**Response shape:** `Data` is the **JSON array of rows** directly — never wrap rows in a `Content` property. Pagination metadata is on the **envelope** (same level as `Success`, `Message`, `Data`):

| Envelope field | Value |
|----------------|-------|
| `Page` | Zero-based page index returned |
| `Size` | Page size returned |
| `TotalCount` | Total matching rows across all pages |

Non-paged responses omit `Page`/`Size`/`TotalCount` (null / absent).

```json
{
  "Success": true,
  "Message": "Users loaded",
  "Page": 0,
  "Size": 20,
  "TotalCount": 9,
  "Data": [ { "UserId": "…", "EmailId": "…" } ],
  "Timestamp": "2026-06-06T12:00:00Z"
}
```

Use `EntityListResponseSupport.ok(message, items, page, size, totalCount)` in controllers. Service layer may still use internal `Paged{Entity}ListDto` types; unwrap `.getContent()` at the controller boundary only.

```java
@GetMapping(produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
public ResponseEntity<StandardApiResponse<List<MedicalDepartmentResponse>>> list(…) {
    PagedMedicalDepartmentListDto paged = service.listPaged(page, size, query, locale);
    return EntityListResponseSupport.ok(
            "Medical departments loaded",
            paged.getContent(),
            paged.getNumber(),
            paged.getSize(),
            paged.getTotalElements());
}
```

## 2. Save (upsert) — `POST /api/v1/{entityName}/save`

Create **or** update one row keyed by the entity's **business key**.

- **Business key:** The natural identifier declared per entity (usually `ExternalId` UUID; may be `Code`, `Slug`, etc.). Document it on the service class.
- **Upsert:** Service loads by business key → merge non-null request fields → save. Missing key → insert.
- **Partial updates:** Omitted/null fields must not wipe existing DB values unless the DTO explicitly allows clear semantics.
- **i18n:** Entities with per-locale copy accept nested locale message arrays/maps in the save body; persist one row per supported locale (`en`, `hi`), fallback to `en`. Reference: `MedicalDepartmentService.createOrUpdate` + `notification_event_rule_messages`.
- **Response:** `200` with saved `{Entity}Response` in `Data`; localized success `Message`. Validation → `400` + `{ENTITY}_SAVE_INVALID`.

```java
@PostMapping(value = "/save", consumes = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE, produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
public ResponseEntity<StandardApiResponse<MedicalDepartmentResponse>> save(
        @RequestBody MedicalDepartmentSaveRequest request,
        HttpServletRequest servletRequest) { … }
```

Prefer **`/save`** over separate `/create`, `/update`, `/createOrUpdate` for new work. Legacy paths may remain until migrated.

**Mandatory:** Every persisted entity below must expose `POST …/save` on its **v1 base path**. If a **legacy base path** also exists, add `POST {legacyBase}/save` with the same upsert semantics (delegate to the same service method). When auditing or touching entities, grep controllers for `/save` — add it if missing before finishing.

## Entity inventory (hospital backend)

| Entity | v1 `POST …/save` | Legacy `POST …/save` | Notes |
|--------|------------------|----------------------|-------|
| User | `/api/v1/users/save` | `/api/user/save` | |
| Medical department | `/api/v1/medical-departments/save` | `/api/medical-department/save`, `/api/Em/save` | |
| Appointment | `/api/v1/appointments/save` | `/api/appointment/save` | multipart create/update legacy paths remain |
| Doctor schedule | `/api/v1/doctor-schedules/save` | `/api/doctor/schedule/save` | |
| Patient prescription | `/api/v1/patient-prescriptions/save` | — | metadata upsert; file create via `POST …/upload` |
| Patient device reading | `/api/v1/patient-device-readings/save` | — | |
| Notification rule (admin) | `/api/v1/notification-rules/save` | `/api/v1/admin/notification-rules/save` | |
| Domain action event (admin) | `/api/v1/domain-action-events/save` | `/api/v1/admin/domain-action-events/save` | |
| UI metadata (singleton) | — | `/api/uiMetdata/save` | fixed id; see `extensibility.mdc` |
| Notification (inbox row) | — | — | **Exempt** — system-generated; read/mark-read only |
| Structured e-prescription | — | — | **Exempt** — appointment workflow actions (`ensure-draft`, `finalize`) |

When touching a legacy entity that lacks these endpoints, **add them** alongside existing routes; deprecate duplicates in a follow-up rather than breaking callers silently.

## 3. Delete — `DELETE /api/v1/{entityName}/{businessKey}`

Remove (or soft-delete) the row identified by `{businessKey}`.

- **Medical / PII entities:** Soft-delete only (`deleted_at`, `@SQLDelete` + `@Where`) — never hard-delete prescriptions, appointments, or patient records.
- **Response:** `200` + localized success `Message`; `Data` null. Not found → `404` + `{ENTITY}_NOT_FOUND`.
- **Auth:** `@PreAuthorize` + audit for sensitive deletes.

```java
@DeleteMapping(value = "/{businessKey}", produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
public ResponseEntity<StandardApiResponse<Void>> delete(@PathVariable String businessKey) { … }
```

## Layering (Spring)

Controller → `{Entity}Service` → `{Entity}Access` / JPA repository. No business logic in controllers. DTOs under `dto/request|response`; never return JPA entities. After Java changes: `cd backend-hospital && gradle compileJava`.

## Clients (Vue / mobile / packages)

- Add list/save/delete methods in the domain service layer (`services/domain/…`, `hospital-api-client`).
- Send `Accept-Language` on every call; display envelope `Message` as returned.
- Parse PascalCase wire keys; map to internal camelCase in one parser module.
- For entity list GET: read pagination from envelope `Page`, `Size`, `TotalCount` via `parsePagedEntityList(body, parser)`.

## Exemptions

Do **not** force this trio on:

- Auth/token flows (`/api/auth/*`), webhooks, file/stream endpoints, idempotent **actions** (`…/join-call`, `…/publish`)
- Aggregates or read-only catalogs with no mutable row
- Singleton config rows that intentionally use a fixed id (e.g. `uiMetdata`) — still use `GET` + `POST …/save` + `DELETE /{id}` but pagination/query may be no-ops

**Legacy paginated list routes** (e.g. `GET /api/user` without `userId`, `GET /api/admin/appointments`) must use the **same list response contract** as v1: `Data` = row array; `Page`/`Size`/`TotalCount` on the envelope via `EntityListResponseSupport.ok(...)`. Never expose internal `Paged{Entity}ListDto` or Spring `Page` wrappers on the wire.

**Legacy save/delete aliases** — when a legacy base path exists, add `POST …/save` and `DELETE …/{businessKey}` alongside v1 (see **Entity inventory** above). Do not remove legacy create/update/delete until callers migrate.

## Checklist (new entity)

- [ ] `GET /api/v1/{entityName}` with `page`/`size` defaults and `{Entity}QueryDto`; **`Data` = row array**; envelope **`Page`/`Size`/`TotalCount`**
- [ ] `POST /api/v1/{entityName}/save` upsert by business key (+ i18n if applicable); **legacy base `/save` if legacy path exists**
- [ ] `DELETE /api/v1/{entityName}/{businessKey}` (soft-delete when required)
- [ ] `{Entity}SaveRequest`, `{Entity}Response` with `@JsonProperty` PascalCase (internal `Paged{Entity}ListDto` optional in services)
- [ ] Stable `ErrorCode` values; localized messages via bundle/DB
- [ ] Client service methods + types in `hospital-api-client` or app services
